# Wallet integration environment.
#
# All three NEXT_PUBLIC_ values below are read by the browser bundle and are
# public by design. The remaining names document the server seam that
# `src/features/wallet/server/wallet.ts` is replaced through; nothing else here
# is wired yet.
#
# Do not add values to this file, and never commit provider credentials.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WEB3AUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WEB3AUTH_NETWORK=sapphire-devnet
# Solana cluster: `solana-devnet` (default) or `solana-mainnet-beta`.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLET_NETWORK=solana-devnet
# Optional. Overrides the public Solana RPC endpoint. The websocket target is
# derived from it, so give a full `https://` URL.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SOLANA_RPC_URL=
#
# Server-only. Never give this a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix. Belongs to the API's token
# verification, not the browser.
# METAMASK_EMBEDDED_WALLET_CLIENT_SECRET=
#
# Server-only. Origin of the Inverge API that exchanges the provider token and
# answers `/auth/me`. No default is assumed: with this unset, sign-in reports that
# the account service is not configured rather than calling a guessed port. The
# API and the web app cannot share a port, so run one of them elsewhere. Set the
# origin only; the server client appends the API's `/api/v1` prefix.
# INVERGE_API_URL=http://localhost:3000
#
# Still unwired:
# WALLET_ONRAMP_PROVIDER=
# WALLET_ONRAMP_API_KEY=
# WALLET_REFUND_SERVICE_URL=
#
# Advertising.
#
# The master switch. Unset means "on in development, off in production"; an
# explicit `false` wins everywhere. With this off no placement renders, in the
# admin preview or in public pages. See docs/ADVERTISING.md.
# INVERGE_ADS_ENABLED=false
#
# Third-party advertising (AdSense). Needs the switch *and* a client id; both
# are required, so copying one line cannot enable a vendor by accident. The
# client id is public by design. The slot id is also public. Never put a
# publisher secret here.
# INVERGE_ADS_THIRD_PARTY_ENABLED=false
# NEXT_PUBLIC_INVERGE_ADSENSE_CLIENT_ID=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_INVERGE_ADSENSE_SLOT_ID=
#
# Paid-placement measurement. Off by default and independent of the inventory
# switch. Both the server kind and the public kind must be `true`, and the
# reader must also opt in at /advertising-preferences. There is no analytics
# sink in this build: `/api/advertising/events` validates and acknowledges
# events with `persisted: false`. Do not describe measurement as operational.
# INVERGE_ADS_ANALYTICS_ENABLED=false
# NEXT_PUBLIC_INVERGE_ADS_ANALYTICS_ENABLED=false
